  "id": "fmea",
  "term": "FMEA",
  "definition": "FMEA, or Failure Modes and Effects Analysis, is a risk assessment method used to identify possible failures and judge their impact. In the supplied source, it is described as a conventional approach that rates risk using occurrence, severity, and detectability, and serves as the basis for a more detailed variant called FMEA+.",
